flowchart TD
    accTitle: Zettings workspace crate dependency graph
    accDescr {
      The Rust workspace is a five-layer directed acyclic graph. zettings-core
      sits at the bottom with no internal dependencies. zettings-search and
      zettings-polkit depend only on core. zettings-backends depends on core
      and polkit. zettings-bridge depends on core, search, backends, and polkit,
      and is the only crate that talks to QML. The application shell under
      apps/zettings consumes zettings-bridge plus the Qt 6 runtime through CMake.
    }

    subgraph workspace["Cargo workspace (virtual manifest)"]
        direction TB
        CORE["zettings-core<br/>registry types · routes · capabilities · errors"]
        SEARCH["zettings-search<br/>index · ranking pipeline"]
        POLKIT["zettings-polkit<br/>authorization gateway"]
        BACKENDS["zettings-backends<br/>D-Bus adapters"]
        BRIDGE["zettings-bridge<br/>cxx-qt QObject bridges"]
    end

    subgraph qt["Qt 6 / QML side (CMake)"]
        APP["apps/zettings<br/>executable + QML modules"]
        QMLUI["QML: Shell · Pages · Components · Style"]
    end

    SEARCH --> CORE
    POLKIT --> CORE
    BACKENDS --> CORE
    BACKENDS --> POLKIT
    BRIDGE --> CORE
    BRIDGE --> SEARCH
    BRIDGE --> BACKENDS
    BRIDGE --> POLKIT
    APP --> BRIDGE
    APP --> QMLUI

    DBUS[("System D-Bus daemons<br/>timedate1 · NetworkManager · BlueZ ·<br/>UPower · power-profiles · login1 · PulseAudio")]
    BACKENDS -. "zbus" .-> DBUS
